AVFormatContext AVOptions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -avioflags flags     (default 0)
                           values:
                             direct  ED......... reduce buffering
    -probesize int64     set probing size (from 32 to I64_MAX) (default
                         5000000)
    -formatprobesize int number of bytes to probe file format (from 0 to
                         2.14748e+09) (default 1048576)
    -fflags flags        (default autobsf)
                           values:
                             ignidx          .D......... ignore index
                             genpts          .D......... generate pts
                             nofillin        .D......... do not fill in
                                             missing values that can be
                                             exactly calculated
                             noparse         .D......... disable AVParsers,
                                             this needs nofillin too
                             igndts          .D......... ignore dts
                             discardcorrupt  .D......... discard corrupted
                                             frames
                             sortdts         .D......... try to interleave
                                             outputted packets by dts
                             fastseek        .D......... fast but inaccurate
                                             seeks
                             nobuffer        .D......... reduce the latency
                                             introduced by optional
                                             buffering
    -seek2any boolean    allow seeking to non-keyframes on demuxer level
                         when supported (default false)
    -analyzeduration int64 specify how many microseconds are analyzed to
                         probe the input (from 0 to I64_MAX) (default 0)
    -cryptokey binary    decryption key
    -indexmem int        max memory used for timestamp index (per stream)
                         (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 1048576)
    -rtbufsize int       max memory used for buffering real-time frames
                         (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 3041280)
    -fdebug flags        print specific debug info (default 0)
                           values:
                             ts  ED.........
    -max_delay int       maximum muxing or demuxing delay in microseconds
                         (from -1 to INT_MAX) (default -1)
    -fpsprobesize int    number of frames used to probe fps (from -1 to
                         2.14748e+09) (default -1)
    -f_err_detect flags  set error detection flags (deprecated; use
                         err_detect, save via avconv) (default crccheck)
                           values:
                             crccheck    .D......... verify embedded CRCs
                             bitstream   .D......... detect bitstream
                                         specification deviations
                             buffer      .D......... detect improper
                                         bitstream length
                             explode     .D......... abort decoding on minor
                                         error detection
                             ignore_err  .D......... ignore errors
                             careful     .D......... consider things that
                                         violate the spec, are fast to check
                                         and have not been seen in the wild
                                         as errors
                             compliant   .D......... consider all spec non
                                         compliancies as errors
                             aggressive  .D......... consider things that a
                                         sane encoder shouldn't do as an
                                         error
    -err_detect flags    set error detection flags (default crccheck)
                           values:
                             crccheck    .D......... verify embedded CRCs
                             bitstream   .D......... detect bitstream
                                         specification deviations
                             buffer      .D......... detect improper
                                         bitstream length
                             explode     .D......... abort decoding on minor
                                         error detection
                             ignore_err  .D......... ignore errors
                             careful     .D......... consider things that
                                         violate the spec, are fast to check
                                         and have not been seen in the wild
                                         as errors
                             compliant   .D......... consider all spec non
                                         compliancies as errors
                             aggressive  .D......... consider things that a
                                         sane encoder shouldn't do as an
                                         error
    -use_wallclock_as_timestamps boolean use wallclock as timestamps
                         (default false)
    -skip_initial_bytes int64 set number of bytes to skip before reading
                         header and frames (from 0 to I64_MAX) (default 0)
    -correct_ts_overflow boolean correct single timestamp overflows (default
                         true)
    -f_strict int        how strictly to follow the standards (deprecated;
                         use strict, save via avconv) (from INT_MIN to
                         INT_MAX) (default normal)
                           values:
                             very          2 ED......... strictly conform to
                                           a older more strict version of
                                           the spec or reference software
                             strict        1 ED......... strictly conform to
                                           all the things in the spec no
                                           matter what the consequences
                             normal        0 ED.........
                             unofficial    -1 ED......... allow unofficial
                                           extensions
                             experimental  -2 ED......... allow
                                           non-standardized experimental
                                           variants
    -strict int          how strictly to follow the standards (from INT_MIN
                         to INT_MAX) (default normal)
                           values:
                             very          2 ED......... strictly conform to
                                           a older more strict version of
                                           the spec or reference software
                             strict        1 ED......... strictly conform to
                                           all the things in the spec no
                                           matter what the consequences
                             normal        0 ED.........
                             unofficial    -1 ED......... allow unofficial
                                           extensions
                             experimental  -2 ED......... allow
                                           non-standardized experimental
                                           variants
    -max_ts_probe int    maximum number of packets to read while waiting for
                         the first timestamp (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default
                         50)
    -dump_separator string set information dump field separator (default ",
                         ")
    -codec_whitelist string List of decoders that are allowed to be used
    -format_whitelist string List of demuxers that are allowed to be used
    -protocol_whitelist string List of protocols that are allowed to be used
    -protocol_blacklist string List of protocols that are not allowed to be
                         used
    -max_streams int     maximum number of streams (from 0 to INT_MAX)
                         (default 1000)
    -skip_estimate_duration_from_pts boolean skip duration calculation in
                         estimate_timings_from_pts (default false)
    -max_probe_packets int Maximum number of packets to probe a codec (from
                         0 to INT_MAX) (default 2500)

