                         streams (default false)
    -reconnect_delay_max int max reconnect delay in seconds after which to
                         give up (from 0 to 4294) (default 120)
    -listen int          listen on HTTP (from 0 to 2) (default 0)
    -short_seek_size int Threshold to favor readahead over seek. (from 0 to
                         INT_MAX) (default 0)

Rtmp AVOptions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    -rtmp_app string     Name of application to connect to on the RTMP
                         server
    -rtmp_buffer int     Set buffer time in milliseconds. The default is
                         3000. (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 3000)
    -rtmp_conn string    Append arbitrary AMF data to the Connect message
    -rtmp_flashver string Version of the Flash plugin used to run the SWF
                         player.
    -rtmp_live int       Specify that the media is a live stream. (from
                         INT_MIN to INT_MAX) (default any)
                           values:
                             any       -2 .D......... both
                             live      -1 .D......... live stream
                             recorded  0 .D......... recorded stream
    -rtmp_pageurl string URL of the web page in which the media was
                         embedded. By default no value will be sent.
    -rtmp_playpath string Stream identifier to play or to publish
    -rtmp_subscribe string Name of live stream to subscribe to. Defaults to
                         rtmp_playpath.
    -rtmp_swfhash binary SHA256 hash of the decompressed SWF file (32
                         bytes).
    -rtmp_swfsize int    Size of the decompressed SWF file, required for
                         SWFVerification. (from 0 to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -rtmp_swfurl string  URL of the SWF player. By default no value will be
                         sent
    -rtmp_swfverify string URL to player swf file, compute hash/size
                         automatically.
    -rtmp_tcurl string   URL of the target stream. Defaults to
                         proto://host[:port]/app.
    -rtmp_listen int     Listen for incoming rtmp connections (from INT_MIN
                         to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -listen int          Listen for incoming rtmp connections (from INT_MIN
                         to INT_MAX) (default 0)
    -tcp_nodelay int     Use TCP_NODELAY to disable Nagle's algorithm (from
                         0 to 1) (default 0)
    -timeout int         Maximum timeout (in seconds) to wait for incoming
                         connections. -1 is infinite. Implies -rtmp_listen 1
                         (from INT_MIN to INT_MAX) (default -1)

